 "news": {
  "date": "2026-10-28",
  "asof": "2026-10-29 11:17 UTC",
  "headline": "The Fed held with two dissents for a hike \u2014 and Alphabet missed, trading below your stop after hours",
  "standfirst": "The Fed held at 3.75-4.00% on a 10-2 vote, with Cook and Hammack dissenting for a hike; the statement called growth strong and inflation elevated, and the ten-year rose 5.2bp to 5.044% while the two-year barely moved. Stocks edged up \u2014 S&P +0.28%, a third straight gain \u2014 and WTI rose 2.9% to $102.78 on a claimed strike on Saudi Arabia's largest refinery. After the close Alphabet missed on revenue and earnings for the first time in nearly four years \u2014 EPS $2.12 against about $3.02, free cash flow minus $9.07bn despite Cloud growth of 103% \u2014 and fell about 9% after hours, while Microsoft rose about 2.6% on Azure growth of 48%. In the book GOOG rose 1.60% to 321.89 in the session at -0.20R, then traded near 293.81 after hours, below the 305.67 stop. The day +5.06; Q4 +30.67 with +34.64 realised.",
  "themes": [
   {
    "kicker": "What's next",
    "right": "Thursday: PCE, Amazon, and Alphabet's open",
